{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03426",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.5,
      "end_seconds": 6.84,
      "duration_seconds": 6.34,
      "text": "All set here, doctor. Chart's updated, and I'll read the readings out when you're ready."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.03,
      "end_seconds": 11.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "Thanks, that's helpful. Hello, please sit. What's been happening?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.99,
      "end_seconds": 24.21,
      "duration_seconds": 11.22,
      "text": "I've been dealing with sudden severe pain in the lower tummy. I didn't want to make a fuss, you know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 28.58,
      "end_seconds": 30.44,
      "duration_seconds": 1.86,
      "text": "When did this begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.26,
      "end_seconds": 33.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "About... well, three weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.48,
      "end_seconds": 37.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "Okay, how often do you get it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.26,
      "end_seconds": 56.93,
      "duration_seconds": 18.67,
      "text": "It's every other day. Oh, and collapsing. Ah, I've had shoulder tip pain too, for about three months. About shoulder tip pain, it happens a couple of times a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 73.44,
      "end_seconds": 77.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "Have you had any discharge, fever or vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 79.2,
      "end_seconds": 84.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "I haven't had discharge, fever or vomiting, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.09,
      "end_seconds": 88.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.08,
      "end_seconds": 91.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "No, that's all fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.36,
      "end_seconds": 96.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "Okay, how about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.68,
      "end_seconds": 101.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "Ah, no, nothing with my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.7,
      "end_seconds": 107.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "Any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 108.99,
      "end_seconds": 120.63,
      "duration_seconds": 11.64,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, I had a reaction to amoxicillin when I was younger, hives, and I've avoided it since."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.34,
      "end_seconds": 125.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "Alright, is there any regular medication you use?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.33,
      "end_seconds": 128.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "No, nothing at the moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.36,
      "end_seconds": 134.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "Tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.84,
      "end_seconds": 137.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "I have acid reflux."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.93,
      "end_seconds": 142.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Right, and alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.45,
      "end_seconds": 146.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "I only drink at family occasions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 151.37,
      "end_seconds": 153.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "How are your meals?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.31,
      "end_seconds": 158.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.0,
      "end_seconds": 161.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Do you work outside the home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.25,
      "end_seconds": 167.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.72,
      "text": "I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.58,
      "end_seconds": 171.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "Do you do any exercise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.06,
      "end_seconds": 175.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "I swim twice a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 188.63,
      "end_seconds": 200.4,
      "duration_seconds": 11.77,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Saturation 99 percent, blood pressure 99 over 63. Respiratory rate 20, pulse is 97 beats a minute, temperature is 37.1 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.92,
      "end_seconds": 201.82,
      "duration_seconds": 0.9,
      "text": "Alright, thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.86,
      "end_seconds": 206.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "I'll examine you in a second, make yourself comfortable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 207.95,
      "end_seconds": 208.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.01,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.51,
      "end_seconds": 211.91,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "Does that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.53,
      "end_seconds": 227.72,
      "duration_seconds": 7.19,
      "text": "You are pale and clammy with a rigid, tender tummy and a very low blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 231.93,
      "end_seconds": 234.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "Good, you can sit up again."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.56,
      "end_seconds": 248.77,
      "duration_seconds": 7.21,
      "text": "So, based on the history and the examination, I'd lean towards a ruptured ectopic pregnancy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 250.03,
      "end_seconds": 252.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "Is it dangerous, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.2,
      "end_seconds": 262.49,
      "duration_seconds": 8.29,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with a ruptured ectopic pregnancy do well once it's treated properly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 263.25,
      "end_seconds": 267.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "I've already done a pregnancy test, it's ready for you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.41,
      "end_seconds": 293.9,
      "duration_seconds": 25.49,
      "text": "Right, thanks, I'll have a look. Let's book urgent blood tests to look into internal bleeding. I am calling the emergency team, you need an operation now. Let's get you seen by the emergency team, I'll arrange the letter. I'll want another look straight away. Right, that's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 295.76,
      "end_seconds": 302.02,
      "duration_seconds": 6.26,
      "text": "Well, uh, okay, that makes sense. Thanks for explaining."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 305.77,
      "end_seconds": 306.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.22,
      "text": "See you soon."
    }
  ]
}